# q065 orders_by_current_customer_segment_dataset
# Intent: E2 join+flag slice-1.5. Order⋈Customer with a DIM flag `?c edw:isCurrent true`
#   on the joined DimCustomer, grouped by the customer segment. Before E2 the join
#   fold declined on ANY star_constraints (the blanket O1 guard) → materialize. E2
#   APPLIES the dim flag while building the FK→GKey map: a non-current customer's
#   join key never enters the map, so its orders drop, and the fold keeps ONLY
#   current-customer orders — the CONSTRAINED count. Mirrors the deployed #1/#2
#   dim-flag join timeout. The oracle IS the constrained count, so this doubles as
#   the join-path over-count trap (a silent fuse-without-the-flag would count ALL
#   orders by segment and fail this member).
# BI lineage: "How many orders per segment, from current customers only?" (dataset path)
# Predicates verified against enterprise.ttl — FactOrder: customer(->DimCustomer);
#   DimCustomer: isCurrent (xsd:boolean), segment.
# Exec path: query_from() with FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main> (the deployed solo shape).
PREFIX edw: <http://ns.fluree.dev/edw#>
SELECT ?seg (COUNT(?o) AS ?n)
FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main>
WHERE { ?o a edw:Order ; edw:customer ?c .
        ?c edw:isCurrent true ; edw:segment ?seg . }
GROUP BY ?seg
